From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office-wp14 <wp14@office.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] numfmt: decimal and group separators by locale

format_value_in and format_general_fit_in take a NumLocale: the decimal point, the thousands
separator, the sub-second point and the General format follow it (same text, same width).
format_value and format_general_fit are the en-US wrappers, so every existing caller and test is
unchanged; TEXT() stays en-US. An en-US golden over every built-in id and 24 custom codes x 25
values, recorded before the change, pins the old output.
---
 crates/numfmt/src/decimal.rs             |   12 +-
 crates/numfmt/src/lib.rs                 |   32 +-
 crates/numfmt/src/render.rs              |   41 +-
 crates/numfmt/src/tests.rs               |    2 +-
 crates/numfmt/tests/en_us_golden.rs      |   92 ++
 crates/numfmt/tests/en_us_golden.tsv     | 1500 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 crates/numfmt/tests/locale_separators.rs |   61 +
 7 files changed, 1704 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/numfmt/tests/en_us_golden.rs
 create mode 100644 crates/numfmt/tests/en_us_golden.tsv
 create mode 100644 crates/numfmt/tests/locale_separators.rs

